\": \"Mon\",\nL138:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL139:       \"title\": \"Even Other AI Labs Are Rallying Around Anthropic’s Slowdown Proposal\",\nL140:       \"teaser\": \"Dario Amodei's 'We Must Pace the Frontier' pulled Altman, Musk, Hassabis, and Nadella publicly on board with slowing AI down. Between the IPO cynics, the antitrust lawyers, and Beijing's 'Cold War' accusations, the negotiation over AI's next phase just started in earnest.\",\nL141:       \"tags\": [\nL142:         \"policy\",\nL143:         \"models\",\nL144:         \"take\"\nL145:       ],\nL146:       \"durationMin\": 37,\nL147:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14\",\nL148:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14.md\",\nL149:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14.json\",\nL150:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14/transcript.md\"\nL151:     },\nL152:     {\nL153:       \"date\": \"2026-09-13\",\nL154:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL155:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL156:       \"title\": \"10 Ways to Think Bigger with Opportunity AI\",\nL157:       \"teaser\": \"GPT-6 Astra confounds — coders are retreating while new capabilities like games, video pipelines, and 3D go unexplored. A weekend big-think with a dozen thought starters for opportunity AI, plus an interactive companion on the site.\",\nL158:       \"tags\": [\nL159:         \"models\",\nL160:         \"take\"\nL161:       ],\nL162:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL163:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13\",\nL164:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13.md\",\nL165:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13.json\",\nL166:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13/transcript.md\"\nL167:     },\nL168:     {\nL169:       \"date\": \"2026-09-11\",\nL170:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL171:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL172:       \"title\": \"What to Use the Latest AI Tools For\",\nL173:       \"teaser\": \"OpenAI hits a compute wall and pauses $200 Pro plans while a second wave of releases points at two big trends: voice-first interfaces and cheap, good-enough models. NLW rips through eight-plus launches — who each is for and what to actually do with it.\",\nL174:       \"tags\": [\nL175:         \"models\",\nL176:         \"enterprise\",\nL177:         \"compute\"\nL178:       ],\nL179:       \"durationMin\": 32,\nL180:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11\",\nL181:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.md\",\nL182:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.json\",\nL183:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11/transcript.md\"\nL184:     },\nL185:     {\nL186:       \"date\": \"2026-09-10\",\nL187:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL188:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL189:       \"title\": \"Anthropic Researcher Says AI Has Over a 10% Chance of Killing All Humans\",\nL190:       \"teaser\": \"An Anthropic researcher's resignation and a colleague's >10% doom odds went 200-million-views viral. NLW skips the outrage and unpacks why the decade-old x-risk message suddenly landed — and where the conversation should go next.\",\nL191:       \"tags\": [\nL192:         \"models\",\nL193:         \"policy\",\nL194:         \"take\"\nL195:       ],\nL196:       \"durationMin\": 36,\nL197:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10\",\nL198:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.md\",\nL199:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.json\",\nL200:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10/transcript.md\"\nL201:     },\nL202:     {\nL203:       \"date\": \"2026-09-09\",\nL204:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL205:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL206:       \"title\": \"AI Model Month Is Off to a Blistering Start\",\nL207:       \"teaser\": \"Three new models, a personal agent, and a Millennium Prize solve wrapped in a scooping scandal. Model month is delivering capability, cost curves, and drama in equal measure.\",\nL208:       \"tags\": [\nL209:         \"models\",\nL210:         \"business\"\nL211:       ],\nL212:       \"durationMin\": 34,\nL213:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09\",\nL214:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.md\",\nL215:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.json\",\nL216:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09/transcript.md\"\nL217:     },\nL218:     {\nL219:       \"date\": \"2026-09-08\",\nL220:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL221:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL222:       \"title\": \"Why GPT-6 Astra Is So Significant and So Confounding\",\nL223:       \"teaser\": \"GPT-6 Astra is the most significant and confounding release in a long time: benchmarks initially tied its predecessor while one-shot 3D games and hours-long computer use blew minds. The key is that it's an opportunity model, not an efficiency one — it expands what you can do rather than improving what you already do.\",\nL224:       \"tags\": [\nL225:         \"models\",\nL226:         \"take\"\nL227:       ],\nL228:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL229:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08\",\nL230:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.md\",\nL231:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.json\",\nL232:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08/transcript.md\"\nL233:     },\nL234:     {\nL235:       \"date\": \"2026-09-07\",\nL236:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL237:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL238:       \"title\": \"The Multiplayer AI Sprint: Build Your Team’s First Shared Agent\",\nL239:       \"teaser\": \"A Labor Day special: why the next frontier of agents is the shared spaces teams inhabit — with evidence from Every, Claude Tag, OpenClaw, and YC — plus the launch of a free four-week sprint to ship your team's first shared agent.\",\nL240:       \"tags\": [\nL241:         \"enterprise\",\nL242:         \"take\"\nL243:       ],\nL244:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL245:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07\",\nL246:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.md\",\nL247:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.json\",\nL248:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07/transcript.md\"\nL249:     },\nL250:     {\nL251:       \"date\": \"2026-09-06\",\nL252:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL253:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL254:       \"title\": \"How to Build an AI-Native Company Today\",\nL255:       \"teaser\": \"A feature-by-feature tour of what actually makes a company AI-native — Alex Lieberman's 30-point list with NLW's agreements, quibbles, and enterprise field notes, plus the missing 31st feature: someone has to own the result.\",\nL256:       \"tags\": [\nL257:         \"enterprise\",\nL258:         \"take\"\nL259:       ],\nL260:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL261:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06\",\nL262:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.md\",\nL263:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.json\",\nL264:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06/transcript.md\"\nL265:     },\nL266:     {\nL267:       \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\nL268:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL269:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL270:       \"title\": \"How AI Changed This Summer\",\nL271:       \"teaser\": \"A holiday-weekend retrospective: Washington became a release gate, Kimi K3 forced another DeepSeek moment, CFOs got their revenge on tokens, agent management became a field, and the Hugging Face incident fired the warning shot. Somehow, it all still feels like prelude.\",\nL272:       \"tags\": [\nL273:         \"models\",\nL274:         \"policy\",\nL275:         \"enterprise\"\nL276:       ],\nL277:       \"durationMin\": 24,\nL278:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04\",\nL279:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.md\",\nL280:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.json\",\nL281:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04/transcript.md\"\nL282:     },\nL283:     {\nL284:       \"date\": \"2026-09-03\",\nL285:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL286:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL287:       \"title\": \"Agentic Loops for Knowledge Workers\",\nL288:       \"teaser\": \"A hands-on webinar with Nufar Gaspar on loop and graph engineering for knowledge workers: when to loop, how to design a verifiable finish line, and when to compose agents into teams — with a live Claude Code demo.\",\nL289:       \"tags\": [\nL290:         \"enterprise\"\nL291:       ],\nL292:       \"durationMin\": 57,\nL293:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03\",\nL294:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.md\",\nL295:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.json\",\nL296:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03/transcript.md\"\nL297:     },\nL298:     {\nL299:       \"date\": \"2026-09-02\",\nL300:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL301:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL302:       \"title\": \"Why Fable 5.1 Is Worth the Upgrade\",\nL303:       \"teaser\": \"Fable 5.1 is unambiguously state-of-the-art and pitched on price as much as power — but real-world token burn tells a messier story, and the right question is where it fits in your stack. Plus: OpenAI says Astra can find and exploit zero-days on its own.\",\nL304:       \"tags\": [\nL305:         \"models\",\nL306:         \"take\"\nL307:       ],\nL308:       \"durationMin\": 31,\nL309:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02\",\nL310:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.md\",\nL311:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.json\",\nL312:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02/transcript.md\"\nL313:     },\nL314:     {\nL315:       \"date\": \"2026-09-01\",\nL316:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL317:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL318:       \"title\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 Shows Where AI Agents Are Going Next\",\nL319:       \"teaser\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 arrives as a ground-up rework, and its multiplayer shared-agent workspace previews where all agent work is headed. Plus a guardrail-stripped 'crime LLM', Anthropic's security overhaul, OpenAI's $1B ad milestone, and Trump's data center firestorm.\",\nL320:       \"tags\": [\nL321:         \"models\",\nL322:         \"take\",\nL323:         \"policy\"\nL324:       ],\nL325:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL326:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01\",\nL327:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01.md\",\nL328:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01.json\",\nL329:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01/transcript.md\"\nL330:     },\nL331:     {\nL332:       \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\nL333:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL334:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL335:       \"title\": \"How to Navigate the Next Wave of AI Competition\",\nL336:       \"teaser\": \"OpenAI cuts Cursor off, and the pattern from Windsurf to the xAI blocks makes the enterprise lesson unavoidable: the sovereignty conversation now covers harnesses, not just models.\",\nL337:       \"tags\": [\nL338:         \"enterprise\",\nL339:         \"business\",\nL340:         \"take\"\nL341:       ],\nL342:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL343:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31\",\nL344:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31.md\",\nL345:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31.json\",\nL346:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31/transcript.md\"\nL347:     },\nL348:     {\nL349:       \"date\": \"2026-08-29\",\nL350:       \"weekday\": \"Sat\",\nL351:       \"type\": \"longreads\",\nL352:       \"title\": \"How to Start AI Coding If You Haven’t Yet\",\n-------------------------